From 54909bc63059d8e3e971f0ad8eb1983520626ebd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WaleWangPW <396218656@qq.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 18:35:54 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 15/22] fix(task): bind release receipt to worktree_id, gate
 root policy, test exact-bound identity
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The previous composition-fix candidate (eb90182) routed the release
admission through physicaldelete.New, but:
1. the receipt's ResourceID carried the anchor's operation_id instead of
   the v0.88-conventional worktree_id;
2. the release path skipped the central RootPolicy and would accept a
   root-protected path;
3. no test exercised the service end-to-end through the real
   physicaldelete.New + SQLInventorySource composition to verify the
   exact-bound anchor identity, the CAS path, and the no-op
   Mutated=false / Executor=ExecutorNone contract.

- Service populates Resource.ID with req.AnchorWorktreeID so the receipt
  follows the v0.88 ResourceID convention.
- verifyAbsentTargetRelease consults the configured RootPolicy after the
  inventory absence proof succeeds; a root-protected release path fails
  closed with ErrProtectedResource.
- Writerdb accepts both 'reconcile' (canonical TaskResourceCleanupTriggerReconcile)
  and 'archived_resource_reconcile' (historical) so the Task05 v2/v3 seed
  pattern loads via the real SQLInventorySource.
- New terminalReleaseCASRepo performs the exact DB-only CAS with the same
  predicate set the production sqlite writer uses (id, operation_id,
  trigger, state, snapshot_digest, resource_id, anchor_revision, and
  active_scope_key IS NULL).
- New resource_cleanup_terminal_release_real_test.go covers:
    * RealCompositionNoOpSucceeds — end-to-end admission + CAS path,
      asserting the anchor's state / completed_at / revision stay
      byte-equal except for the admitted transition.
    * ReceiptResourceIDIsWorktreeID — sealed admission direct call
      asserting receipt.ResourceID == worktree_id, NOT operation_id.
    * RootPolicyRejectsRootProtectedPath — both the central admission
      and the service-level call fail closed when the target path is
      root-protected.
    * ExactBoundIdentityMismatchFails — four identity-drift mutations
      (operation_id, worktree_id, digest, task_id) all fail closed.
